The '''Melbu''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed in [[the galaxy]]. They were distinguished by their respirator horns, which were connected to a [[Breath mask|breathing mask]] worn on the mouth and their bright orange eyes. [[Auromae Iselo]], a member of the [[Cloud-Riders]], was a Melbu.

==Biology and appearance==
The Melbu were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] that existed in [[the galaxy]]. They were distinguished by their respirator horns, which were connected to a [[Breath mask|breathing mask]] worn on the mouth. They also had [[Color|reddish-brown]] skin and orange [[eye]]s.<ref name="The Official Guide" />

==Melbu in the galaxy==
Melbu could be found on various [[planet]]s throughout the galaxy, including [[Koboh]],<ref name="Jedi Survivor">[[Star Wars Jedi: Survivor]]</ref> [[Nar Shaddaa]],<ref name="WotBH 1">[[War of the Bounty Hunters 1|''War of the Bounty Hunters'' 1]]</ref> and [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Stranger in a Strange Land">{{BOBF|Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land}}</ref>

During the [[Imperial Era]], [[Auromae Iselo]], a member of the species, operated as a [[bounty hunter]] and later joined the [[Cloud-Riders]] and assisted the group in various missions in opposition to the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

[[Wef]], another member of the species, operated as an [[arms dealer]] during the Imperial Era. The arms dealer supplied several clients, including the [[Hidden Hand]] criminal syndicate, and the [[cyborg]] bounty hunter [[Beilert Valance]]'s team.<ref name="Target Vader 3">[[Target Vader 3|''Target Vader'' 3]]</ref>

By the [[time]] of the [[New Republic Era]], a Melbu bounty hunter joined the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]]. During a mission with the Guild, the Melbu lost their life in a [[Incident on Nevarro|skirmish]] with the [[Mandalorian]] [[Din Djarin]].<ref name="Chapter 3">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 3: The Sin}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Melbu species made their debut in the [[2018]] ''[[Star Wars Anthology Series]]'' film ''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]'', directed by [[Ron Howard]].<ref name="Solo" /> The species' design originated from a drawing by the artist [[Jake Lunt Davies]]' daughter. While interpreting her sketch, Davies decided that the horns would be part of the respiratory system consisting of tubes connecting to the mouth.<ref name="Art-Solo">''[[The Art of Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

For the texture of the species' skin, he used squashes and gherkins as inspiration, while the eyes were based off the appearances of amber and other precious stones. The overall color scheme was intentionally chosen in order to be reminiscent of aliens featured on [[1950s]] science fiction covers.<ref name="Art-Solo" />

